WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:20.623
Grandpa put six big sweet potatoes into a sack for Mr. Henderson.

2
00:00:20.624 --> 00:00:26.381
"Two dollars and fifty cents!" said Katie. "And thank you!"

3
00:00:26.382 --> 00:00:30.913
"I'd like three squashes," said Mr. Dexter.

4
00:00:30.914 --> 00:00:34.390
Today was the Willow Creek Harvest Fair.

5
00:00:34.391 --> 00:00:40.245
The whole Donovan family was helping Grandpa sell his garden produce.

6
00:00:40.246 --> 00:00:47.434
Squashes, onions, carrots, apples, radishes, and turnips covered Grandpa's table.

7
00:00:47.435 --> 00:00:50.919
A dozen fat pumpkins sat on the ground.

8
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.942
"Could someone carry a pumpkin to my car?" asked Mrs. Pinker.

9
00:00:55.943 --> 00:01:00.421
"I'd like three apples," said Jeff the mailman.

10
00:01:00.422 --> 00:01:04.346
"How much are your turnips?" asked Mrs. Penkov.

11
00:01:04.347 --> 00:01:08.816
"Where is Joy?" said Mom. "We need help!"

12
00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:13.548
"I saw her over there just a minute ago," said Mr. Henderson.

13
00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:16.881
"She's listening to the country band."

14
00:01:16.882 --> 00:01:20.687
"Katie, run and get her," said Mom.

15
00:01:20.688 --> 00:01:24.191
Katie ran through the crowd in the town park.

16
00:01:24.192 --> 00:01:29.082
She found her sister bouncing to the beat of loud country music.

17
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:31.383
"Joy!" called Katie.

18
00:01:31.384 --> 00:01:35.568
"Mom said to come help at the produce stand!"

19
00:01:35.569 --> 00:01:39.188
Joy was not paying attention to her sister.

20
00:01:39.189 --> 00:01:44.549
When the band played their final notes, she clapped and cheered with the crowd.

21
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:48.313
Then a girl in jean overalls ran onto the stage.

22
00:01:48.314 --> 00:01:51.411
She was carrying a violin.

23
00:01:51.412 --> 00:02:00.017
"Let's all welcome this little fiddler from Kirbyville—Maggie Dowell!" shouted the announcer.

24
00:02:00.018 --> 00:02:03.943
"Look! She's our age," Joy said.

25
00:02:03.944 --> 00:02:10.445
Katie watched as Maggie Dowell lifted her fiddle and started playing an old folk song.

26
00:02:10.446 --> 00:02:14.363
At first she played slowly and gently.

27
00:02:14.364 --> 00:02:17.036
"Tell Mom I'll be right there," said Joy.

28
00:02:17.037 --> 00:02:19.700
"I want to hear one more song."

29
00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:24.188
"Okay," said Katie, but she didn't move either.

30
00:02:24.189 --> 00:02:27.837
Maggie's fiddle playing was getting livelier.

31
00:02:27.838 --> 00:02:31.010
She stomped her right foot to the beat.

32
00:02:31.011 --> 00:02:36.515
Her bow ripped across the strings and sent puffs of dust into the air.

33
00:02:36.516 --> 00:02:40.864
"I wish I could play the fiddle like that!" said Joy.

34
00:02:40.865 --> 00:02:44.152
"Come on, Joy," Katie reminded her sister.

35
00:02:44.153 --> 00:02:50.065
"We're supposed to be helping Grandpa."

36
00:02:50.066 --> 00:02:57.469
Later that afternoon, the Donovans sat at a picnic table eating fried fish and corn on the cob.

37
00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:01.515
"Here comes Aunt Sally and Luke!" said Katie.

38
00:03:01.516 --> 00:03:07.061
"Larry's dad just won the giant pumpkin contest!" said Luke.

39
00:03:07.062 --> 00:03:11.522
"His pumpkin weighed more than one hundred pounds!"

40
00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:16.250
"We sold every one of our pumpkins," said Katie.

41
00:03:16.251 --> 00:03:20.027
"Did you meet your goal?" asked Aunt Sally.

42
00:03:20.028 --> 00:03:22.691
"Yes, we did," said Grandpa.

43
00:03:22.692 --> 00:03:25.880
"We made enough to buy seeds for next year."

44
00:03:25.881 --> 00:03:30.088
"And to get the garden fence repaired," said Dad.

45
00:03:30.089 --> 00:03:33.647
Joy wasn't interested in pumpkins or seeds.

46
00:03:33.648 --> 00:03:39.904
She could talk about only one thing—Maggie Dowell's fiddle playing.

47
00:03:39.905 --> 00:03:43.500
"You should have heard that girl!" she said.

48
00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:47.166
"Yeah! She was great!" said Katie.

49
00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:52.172
She jumped up and wildly played an imaginary fiddle.

50
00:03:52.173 --> 00:03:56.560
Then she plopped back down and picked up her corn on the cob.

51
00:03:56.561 --> 00:03:59.773
"But who wants to practice all the time?"

52
00:03:59.774 --> 00:04:02.596
"I wouldn't mind practicing," said Joy.

53
00:04:02.597 --> 00:04:06.619
"I'd do anything to play like Maggie Dowell."

54
00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:13.154
"Your great-grandma Donovan got her first fiddle when she was no bigger than you," said Grandpa.

55
00:04:13.155 --> 00:04:18.002
"Her daddy went all the way to Bates City and bought her a half-size one.

56
00:04:18.003 --> 00:04:20.368
It was made in Germany."

57
00:04:20.369 --> 00:04:24.653
"I wish you girls had known your great-grandma," said Dad.

58
00:04:24.654 --> 00:04:28.576
"I wish I had heard her play," said Joy.

59
00:04:28.577 --> 00:04:33.221
"Where is that fiddle?" said Grandpa. "In the attic?"

60
00:04:33.222 --> 00:04:36.808
"It might be up there," said Mom.

61
00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.831
Joy's mouth fell open.

62
00:04:38.832 --> 00:04:41.067
"Do you still have it?"

63
00:04:41.068 --> 00:04:43.356
"Oh yes," said Grandpa.

64
00:04:43.357 --> 00:04:46.606
"She never sold that first little fiddle."

65
00:04:46.607 --> 00:04:49.850
"Can we look for it?" said Joy.

66
00:04:49.851 --> 00:04:53.761
"We'll look for it tomorrow morning," said Grandpa.

67
00:04:53.762 --> 00:04:56.898
"Maybe one of you girls would like to try it."

68
00:04:56.899 --> 00:04:59.755
Katie wiped butter dripping from her chin.

69
00:04:59.756 --> 00:05:02.722
"Not me," she said.

70
00:05:02.723 --> 00:05:08.717
"Me!" said Joy.
